#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0388 expect=violation domain=TP
# Rule:Description: TPSTGORD is populated with a value that is not an integer.
#note "Added 2026-09-14 (PLAN-column-type-conformance carried-forward). This rule had NO .cdt scenario at all while its semantics were rewritten from an integer-shaped regex to `not is_integer` — the CORE-000587 shape. TPSTGORD is Num, and on a Num column the retired regex subject now ERRORS under the R9 gate, so this conformant-typed fixture is what distinguishes the migrated rule from the unmigrated one. ⭐ MEASURED 2026-09-14, not argued: restoring `TPSTGORD !~ /^-?[0-9]+$/` reds this file and its -valid- twin with the gate's own message. ⚠ CDISC-SEND-0388 is a SENDIG-DART rule ONLY (1.1 and 1.2 — TP is the DART Trial Paths domain), so the declaration is sendig-dart, not sendig; declaring the wrong standard here would fail the membership assertion rather than run against nothing. Row 1 is a fractional stage order and fires; row 2 is whole and must not."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 TPSEQ=1
dataset TP class="TRIAL DESIGN" label="Trial Paths"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RSTGCD   type=Char label="Repro Stage Code"
col TPSTGORD type=Num  label="Planned Order of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | TP | 1 | F0 | 1.5
S1 | TP | 2 | F1 | 2
---
